// Combat content.
//
// There is very little of it, and that is the design: the engine owns
// hitpoints, hitsplats, the accuracy and max-hit rolls, death, respawn and
// swing timing, because those have to be consistent. What is attackable is not
// content either — it is whatever the cache's own npc record offers an "Attack"
// op for, which is the same test the client's right-click menu makes.
//
// Content decides who is aggressive and how hard they hit, and those live in
// the area's .npc config. What belongs here is anything a fight should *say*.

[opnpc2,goblin]
npc_say("Ye be dead soon!");
